=== the observed hemispheric mean ===
  NOAA GML Carbon Cycle Cooperative Global Air Sampling Network, surface-flask monthly means; https://gml.noaa.gov/aftp/data/trace_gases/co2c13/flask/surface/ Site coordinates from gml.noaa.gov/dv/site.
  87 sites; Marcus 2026-09-22: all sites, latitude-band-area (equal sin-lat, 12 bands/hemisphere) weighted, gaps dropped -- no interpolation, empty bands dropped and weights renormalised. `unweighted` and `coslat` carried for sensitivity to the wording.

=== the model's IMPLIED d13C offset (derived from rep_dC = +3.515 ppm) ===
  NH (MLO): -0.1702 permil   [range -0.1853 to -0.1546 over 1990-2014]
  SH (SPO): -0.1725 permil   [range -0.1853 to -0.1588 over 1990-2014]

=== MEASURED: hemispheric mean MINUS station (permil) ===
    + = the hemispheric mean is HEAVIER (less negative) than the station

  weighting: equalarea     NH -0.0922 (n 300)   SH -0.0106 (n 296)
  weighting: unweighted    NH -0.1119 (n 300)   SH -0.0101 (n 296)
  weighting: coslat        NH -0.0971 (n 300)   SH -0.0059 (n 296)

  primary = equalarea. ⚠ spread across the three weightings is the sensitivity to
     the ruling's wording, not an uncertainty on the atmosphere.

=== 1. DOES THE MODEL'S IMPLIED OFFSET MATCH THE MEASURED ONE? ===
                                         NH           SH
  model implies                     -0.1702      -0.1725
  MEASURED                          -0.0922      -0.0106
  same sign?                            yes          yes
  model / measured                      1.8         16.2

=== the CO2 station offset, from the SAME 87 sites and weighting ===
  NH (MLO): +1.2922 ppm over 312 months, 1989-2014   [MBL reference: +0.738]
  SH (SPO): +0.7865 ppm over 305 months, 1989-2014   [MBL reference: +0.814]

=== 2. ⭐ THE MASS-BALANCE TIE, TESTED AGAINST OBSERVATION ===
  Feed the MEASURED CO2 offset through the model's own formula
  (d_s = LIK_REP_SOURCE_D13C = -26.5 permil, PROVISIONAL and UNCITED):

                                               NH           SH
  predicted from the MEASURED CO2 offset      -0.0628      -0.0387
  MEASURED d13C offset                    -0.0922      -0.0106
  measured / predicted                        1.5          0.3

  source signature that WOULD reconcile        -35.1        -13.2
    (the model assumes)                     -26.5        -26.5

  ⇒ If these agree, the mass-balance tie is corroborated by observation and
    the d13C side of `rep_dC` is over-large for the SAME reason the CO2 side
    is. If they disagree, the TIE is the defect, not just the magnitude --
    and d_s is the uncited constant in it.

  n = 300 (NH) / 296 (SH) matched months, 1989-2014.
